# SOURCE is the main checkout this time, which is safe: it was ON local/mac-scan-fix and clean
# for the whole build, so gate 4 (vcs.revision == build-root HEAD) passed as ade04405b690. The
# worktree warning below still stands for anything built via SYNCTHING_REPO_ROOT.
#
# BUILD ROOTS: a git worktree is NOT a safe build root. Go's vcs stamping run inside a worktree
# records the HEAD of the MAIN checkout, so an artifact built there claims a commit it does not
# contain. That is how the 13d5827d8dfe build ended up reporting a version string from a
# different branch and had no 60-gc-retired.sql at all, so the retirement queue was dead on this
# machine and grew to 5733 entries. build.sh gate 4 refuses any artifact whose vcs.revision
# disagrees with its build root, and gate 5 refuses a vcs.modified=true artifact.

